From: Onuralp SEZER <thunderbirdtr@fedoraproject.org>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: hm1092: Defer probe until the fwnode endpoint exists

On Intel laptops (Dell XPS 14/16 DA14260/DA16260, Panther Lake + IPU7) the
fwnode graph endpoint of the HM1092 is created by ipu-bridge when the IPU
ISYS probes. If the sensor probes first, the endpoint is missing and probe
fails for good with "parsing endpoint failed".

Return -EPROBE_DEFER while the endpoint is missing, the same way ov08x40
and other IPU sensors do.

Not yet upstream; applies on top of "media: i2c: hm1092: Add ACPI
enumeration and the 19.2 MHz configuration".

Signed-off-by: Onuralp SEZER <thunderbirdtr@fedoraproject.org>
---
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/hm1092.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/hm1092.c
@@ -899,7 +899,15 @@
 	unsigned long link_freq_bitmap;
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * On ACPI systems the fwnode graph is created by the IPU bridge driver,
+	 * which also adds the sensor properties. Wait for it.
+	 */
 	ep = fwnode_graph_get_endpoint_by_id(fwnode, 0, 0, 0);
+	if (!ep)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, -EPROBE_DEFER,
+				     "waiting for fwnode graph endpoint\n");
+
 	ret = v4l2_fwnode_endpoint_alloc_parse(ep, &bus_cfg);
 	fwnode_handle_put(ep);
 	if (ret)
